{"slug":"nmap-scanning-workflow","title":"A Practical Nmap Workflow for Lab Machines","date":"2026-10-08","updated":null,"description":"A fast two-stage Nmap workflow for lab targets: find open ports quickly, then run detailed scripts only where it matters, with notes on what each flag does.","category":"tutorial","platform":null,"difficulty":null,"tags":["nmap","enumeration","networking"],"featured":false,"cover":null,"readingTime":1,"html":"<p>Scanning every port with full scripts is slow. A two-stage approach is faster and gives cleaner notes.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-important\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Important</p>\n<p>Scan only systems you own or are authorised to test, such as lab environments.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"stage-1-find-open-ports\">Stage 1: find open ports<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#stage-1-find-open-ports\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">nmap</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -p-</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --min-rate</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> 2000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -T4</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -oN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> scans/all-ports.txt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$TARGET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"stage-2-detail-on-open-ports-only\">Stage 2: detail on open ports only<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#stage-2-detail-on-open-ports-only\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">ports</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">grep</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -oP</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> '^\\d+(?=/tcp\\s+open)'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> scans/all-ports.txt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> paste</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -sd,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">nmap</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -sC</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -sV</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -p</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ports</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -oN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> scans/detail.txt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$TARGET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"flag-reference\">Flag reference<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#flag-reference\">#</a></h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>-p-</code></td><td>Scan all 65535 TCP ports</td></tr><tr><td><code>--min-rate</code></td><td>Send at least this many packets/second</td></tr><tr><td><code>-sC</code></td><td>Run Nmap's default scripts</td></tr><tr><td><code>-sV</code></td><td>Probe service versions</td></tr><tr><td><code>-oN</code></td><td>Save normal output to a file</td></tr><tr><td><code>-sU --top-ports 20</code></td><td>Quick check of common UDP ports</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"reading-the-output\">Reading the output<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#reading-the-output\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">text</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"text\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>80/tcp open  http  nginx 1.18.0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>|_http-title: Did not follow redirect to http://target.htb/</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>A redirect to a hostname is a cue to add an <code>/etc/hosts</code> entry and look for virtual hosts.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-note\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Note</p>\n<p>High scan rates can miss ports on unreliable networks. If results look incomplete, rescan at a lower rate.</p>\n</aside>","toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"stage-1-find-open-ports","text":"Stage 1: find open ports"},{"depth":2,"id":"stage-2-detail-on-open-ports-only","text":"Stage 2: detail on open ports only"},{"depth":2,"id":"flag-reference","text":"Flag reference"},{"depth":2,"id":"reading-the-output","text":"Reading the output"}],"prev":{"slug":"thm-sample-sql-injection-room","title":"Sample THM Writeup: A Login Form and Union-Based SQL Injection"},"next":{"slug":"htb-sample-lantern","title":"Sample HTB Writeup: Lantern (Fictional Linux Box)"},"related":["offsec-lab-methodology-notes"]}